The key points from this module are:
An ethical hacker is a person who hacks into a computer network to test or evaluate its security rather than with malicious or criminal intent.
Ethical hacking refers to the act of locating weaknesses and vulnerabilities of computer and information systems by duplicating the intent and actions of malicious hackers.
A penetration test intends to validate or test the security of any IT system, and the owner of the system must authorise this.
A white-hat hacker is an ethical computer hacker or security expert who specialises in penetration testing and in other testing methodologies that ensures the security of an organisation's information system.
Bash is a UNIX command shell written for the GNU project. Its name is an acronym for Bourne and shell.
Open System Interconnection (OSI) model is the first standard created to rule network communication. It has seven layers.
TCP/IP model, also known as DARPA layers, is the successor of the OSI model, and it is implemented in nearly every communication system. It consists of four layers.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Address Resolution Protocol (ARP) is a way to map IP addresses to the media access control (MAC) address.
Domain Name Service (DNS) works within a hierarchical naming structure. A DNS server that holds resource records for a zone is the authoritative DNS server.
Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP) is a way to perform real-time health checking of all your communication systems.
Cryptography is a way of hiding the meaning of communication.
A cipher is a set of rules or algorithms that defines how to take a plain text and turn it into an unreadable format.
Below are some types of cryptographic algorithms:
Symmetric cryptography: This involves using one key for both encryption and decryption processes. The sender and receiver use the same key.
Asymmetric cryptography: This uses public and private keys that are mathematically related but should not be able to be derived from each other.
Hashing functions: This accepts a variable-length string (message) and generates a fixed-length value (hash value).
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Salting is the process of securing hashes from a rainbow table attack. Password salt makes each hashed password in a database unique.
Denial of service (DoS) is an attack on the availability of IT resources such as a server, network device, website, etc.
In a botnet attack, attackers distribute malware to turn computers into a bot or zombies. These allow intruders to operate remotely.
A computer virus is a program that can copy itself and infect a computer without the permission or knowledge of the user.
A trojan horse is a destructive program that masquerades as a benign application.
A backdoor is a method of bypassing the normal authentication process.
VLANs provide enhanced performance on the network and an additional security layer that can prevent several attacks from infecting the whole network.
Security information and event management(SIEM) combine security information and security event management to provide real-time monitoring and analysis of alerts generated by network devices and applications.
